WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Welcome to our training on how to get paid when selling globally in the Amazon Store.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.226
This video will show you how to receive your net proceeds from your global Amazon stores,

00:00:10.226 --> 00:00:14.300
fast and easy with Amazon Currency Converter for Sellers or ACCS.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.180
You rarely need to think about dealing with different currencies while selling domestically.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.780
This changes however when you expand your business abroad.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.480
Perhaps you've been looking to reach customers in other regions.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.140
Or you've identified a demand for your products in another country.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.400
When you sell globally, your net proceeds are paid out in foreign currencies.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.920
ACCS allows you to receive payments directly in your local bank account in your local currency.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.160
We recommend using ACCS so you don't have to open a foreign bank account

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.400
or rely on a third-party payment service provider.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.040
Here's how ACCS works.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.980
When your disbursement is ready in Seller Central,

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.520
we send it to our bank service providers.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.903
They then convert and deposit your global payments

00:01:01.903 --> 00:01:03.960
into your local bank account directly.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.200
Our bank providers use highly competitive exchange rates similar to the ones used by

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.880
the largest traders on the market.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.440
We don't add any hidden fees or markups.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:21.960
For most of the currencies we support, your only cost is the volume-based ACCS fee.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.066
You will fall within different tiers based on your total cross-currency disbursement

00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:29.220
amount over the past 12 months.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.823
We recalculate your tier every month and apply the volume-based

00:01:33.823 --> 00:01:34.540
fee accordingly.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.960
In short, the more business you do, the lower the ACCS fee you pay.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.540
Another way to lower your fee is to merge all your global stores to move to a higher tier.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.500
Search "Merge Accounts in Seller Central" to learn more.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.104
To sign up for ACCS, open the Settings menu

00:01:53.104 --> 00:01:57.240
in Seller Central by selecting the gear icon in the top right corner.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:03.140
Then click "Account Info" and navigate to "Deposit Methods Under Payment Information."

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.820
If you don't have a deposit method set up for your desired international store in Seller Central,

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.440
select Assign next to that store to add your bank account information.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.020
Then enter your local currency bank account information as the deposit method.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.080
If you've already set up a foreign bank account as a deposit method in your target store,

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.700
replace it with your local currency bank account to start using ACCS.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.260
On the setup page, select your bank location from the drop-down menu.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.393
Note that only regions

00:02:35.393 --> 00:02:38.220
listed in this menu are supported by ACCS.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.140
If your bank isn't located in one of the listed locations,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.720
search for "Payment Service Provider Program in Seller Central" to learn how to proceed.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:54.558
After you fill out the account information, we'll verify any new or changed deposit method on your

00:02:54.558 --> 00:02:54.940
account.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:00.280
Once this process is complete, you can activate the deposit method to receive payments.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:01.600
And that's it!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.440
You can then sit back and receive payments from your global Amazon stores automatically.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.060
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
